    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a high-leverage slate today, with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.27) and **Trea Turner** (66.41) serving as our primary offensive engines. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our highest-graded play; his matchup against a favorable 4.62 xERA arm, combined with his top-of-the-order positioning and elite sprint speed, makes him the premier catalyst for our scarcity-driven SB strategy. Similarly, **Trea Turner** remains an elite start, as the opposing battery\u2019s slow delivery significantly mitigates the risk posed by their catcher\u2019s pop time, keeping his theft probability high. We also look for **Yordan Alvarez** (66.32) to provide stability; despite the L/L disadvantage, his elite xwOBA of 0.450 outweighs the platoon friction, ensuring he remains a focal point of our middle-of-the-order production.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today was benching **Carson Benge** (38.60). While he offered decent base projections, his matchup against a sub-3.00 xERA starter suppressed his ceiling below our 40.0 efficiency floor, forcing us to prioritize the platoon advantages of **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Junior Caminero**. Caution is warranted with **Caleb Durbin** (51.03); as his lineup status remains pending, we have modeled him in the #6 hole. His score is also slightly compressed due to an elite defensive opponent whose arm makes stealing opportunistic rather than guaranteed. We are playing a disciplined game today\u2014avoiding below-floor candidates like **Carson Benge** while leaning heavily on the speed-oriented, high-order anchors in **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Trea Turner** to maximize our daily R and SB output.",
